From 43494ef05536554f928ddd6813a584f982483cd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:42:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HermOS V5 Beta: immediate-mode desktop scene matching the
 design sheet

Replace the per-widget painters in desktop_builder with a scene renderer
(scene_gfx.h / scene.h / scene_windows.h) that draws the whole Shiro desktop
from analytic shapes: header, greeting, a single search field, navigation
rail, Agents & Workers panel, taskbar, left dock and the six windows.

Root causes fixed:
- Scrambled text: STBTT_malloc was nullptr, so glyph bitmaps were never
  written. Now an arena allocator, shared with the legacy FontRenderer.
- Duplicate search bar: wallpaper.png was a damaged mock-up crop with UI
  baked in. Replaced with clean scenery plus a water reflection.
- Theme geometry was overridden by a fixed 3x2 grid (_compute_grid).

Theme engine: geometry in 1/10000 of the screen (scale: 10000) and a new
<panels> section (left/bottom: visible | autohide | hidden).

Hideable left dock and bottom bar use a Plasma-style panel model (edge,
thickness, mode, ease-out-cubic reveal advanced by elapsed time, clientArea
struts). Hover the left edge, Meta+L, Meta+B, or click the grip tab.

Also: Inter (OFL) fonts, compass and hydroponics assets, run-script
changes, a host preview tool (tools/scene_preview) and doc/SCENE.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PFnR3vwQxhPvBkACnmcidX
